Upstream 1C rules
-----------------

This profile vendors and adapts material from comol/ai_rules_1c
(https://github.com/comol/ai_rules_1c). The pin is recorded in
`upstream.lock.json` and the human register is `UPSTREAM-REGISTER.md`.

Upstream terms are those stated in that repository’s README (currently
informal wording on GitHub; not a named OSI license). This overlay — Pi
PLAN/BUILD, command catalog, MCP opt-in, Docker policy, `/review-airules`
— is separate from the upstream 1C coding ruleset.

Redistributing a full vendored upstream snapshot must also follow any
package `UPSTREAM-LICENSE-NOTICE` shipped with pi-1c-agent.

Lab extras and third-party skills
---------------------------------

Lab extras in this profile (`skills/vanessa-mcp`, `kd2-rules`,
`kd31-rules`, `1c-mcp-toolkit`) are author-owned beta snapshots. They
adapt third-party MIT skill text from Desko77/cursor-1c-skills
(https://github.com/Desko77/cursor-1c-skills) and depend at runtime on
third-party products that are **referenced, not vendored**:

- Vanessa Automation (Pr-Mex)
- neurofish client MCP (`client_mcp.cfe`)
- ROCTUP MCP_Toolkit.epf

They are not `comol/ai_rules_1c`.

`skills/humanizer-ru` is a snapshot of Comol Humanizer_RU
(https://github.com/comol/Humanizer_RU, MIT) plus this author’s
knowledge/overlay. It is not the English humanizer skill and is not
synced via `/review-airules`.

